*> IC117M -- middle module of the NIST COBOL-85 "CALL without USING phrase"
*> chain (IC116M -> IC117M -> IC118M). Here IC117M is compiled as the
*> program under test and its own `CALL "IC118M"` is the mocked boundary.
*>
*> USNG-TEST-03 is the paragraph that issues `CALL "IC118M"`; driving it in
*> isolation keeps the run clear of the CCVS print-file paragraphs.
TESTSUITE "IC117M CALL without USING phrase"

TESTCASE "USNG-TEST-03 calls subprogram IC118M (mocked)"
    MOCK CALL "IC118M"
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM USNG-TEST-03
    VERIFY CALL "IC118M" WAS CALLED ONCE
